  "note": "The most physical book in the Studios: a lonely inn on a cove, Bristol docks, a ship at sea, an island. Every gun comes twice — near (sharp, dry, loud) and far (muffled, late, long echo) — and most of the shooting is far. Part One is the Admiral Benbow: the surf below the cliff, the parlour fire, the stick on the frozen road, the riders on the hill. Shared sounds are borrowed from Dracula by URL.",
